# Rules whose empty space does not stay empty (Critters, Tron) and "hide vacuum fluctuations".
# Expects the default start-up: a blob of 1210 cells on 256×256.
wait 25; expect_population 1210

# A rule taken up on an odd generation starts its vacuum's cycle there: nothing is inverted.
step 1; rule critters; wait 3; shot vacuum-1-critters-at-generation-1
# One step later the empty world is all alive. What is stored is the pattern without its
# vacuum, so the cells and their count know nothing of it ...
step 1; wait 3; expect_population 1210; shot vacuum-2-hidden
# ... and only the unhidden view shows the automaton as it is.
vacuum off; wait 3; shot vacuum-3-unhidden; vacuum on

# The next rule gets the pattern as drawn, wherever the vacuum was in its cycle.
rule single-rotation; wait 3; expect_population 1210; shot vacuum-4-back-to-single-rotation

# Painting stores what is drawn, also while the vacuum is all alive.
clear; rule critters; step 1; fit; wait 3; expect_population 0
drag Grid 60 0; wait 2; expect_cell 128 128 on; shot vacuum-5-painted
press Shift; drag Grid 60 0; release Shift; wait 2; expect_population 0
quit
